From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ucm2: Rockchip: Add ES8388 and RK3588 HDMI/DP configurations

Add UCM for two kinds of simple-audio-card found on RK3588 boards:

- "rockchip,es8388": an ES8388 codec (ES8328 driver) on the analog jack,
  as on the Orange Pi 5, 5B and 5 Pro and the Firefly ROC-RK3588S-PC.
  The codec comes out of reset with the DAC at -96 dB and both output
  stages at -30 dB, so nothing is audible until the mixer is set up. The
  BootSequence brings the DAC and LOUT1/ROUT1 to 0 dB, selects stereo
  routing, turns the analog input bypass off and sets up the on-board
  microphone (LINPUT2/RINPUT2). The Headphones device uses the "Headphones
  Jack" control when the card has one (simple-audio-card,hp-det-gpios);
  the Mic and Headset (LINPUT1/RINPUT1) devices conflict, since both use
  the same ADC.

- "hdmi0", "hdmi1", "dp0": the HDMI and DisplayPort cards that
  rk3588-base.dtsi and rk3588-extra.dtsi define for the DW HDMI QP and
  DW DP controllers. They have no mixer controls; the profile only gives
  the outputs a name ("HDMI" or "DisplayPort") and a priority, so that
  they no longer all show up as "Built-in Audio".

Tested on an Orange Pi 5 with alsaucm and PipeWire 1.6 (ACP): both
cards get their HiFi profiles, HDMI plays, the ES8388 profile follows the
jack control, and alsactl init applies the boot sequence on first boot.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
